+# Hy3-FP8 on one trn3 node: 85k shared-prefix workload under a latency SLO
+
+`scripts/serve_85k_trn3.sh` serves Hy3-FP8 on one trn3 node (TP=64, EP=64, LNC=2), with prefill and decode on the
+same server. `scripts/bench_85k_slo.sh` measures it.
+
+## Workload and SLO
+
+- Every request is the 78,336-token shared prefix of `bench_data/prefix` plus its own suffix: 85,000 input tokens and
+  1024 output tokens (`ignore_eos`), sampled at temperature 0.9.
+- The benchmark runs a closed loop at concurrency C, with 10 x C requests per point.
+- SLO: TTFT P50 < 7 s, TPOT P50 < 20 ms, and a prefix-cache hit rate above 92% (from the server's `/metrics`).
+  P90 values are reported as well.
+- The metric is output tok/s at the highest C at which the SLO holds.
+
+## Configuration
+
+FP8 KV with the 448-range trn3 profile (`kv_profiles/Hy3-FP8_mtp_neuron_trn3.safetensors`), MTP k=3, sparse
+prefill and sparse decode attention at 0.0625, max_model_len 87040 and max_num_seqs 24. The prefill buckets go up to
+8192, so the ~6.7k-token suffix of a request is one prefill chunk. The decode buckets are [1, 8, 16, 20, 24].
+
+| Area | Flags | What they do |
+|---|---|---|
+| Prefill experts | `HY3_MOE_CTE_MX` `HY3_MOE_CTE_NO_REDUCE` `HY3_MOE_CTE_SKIP_WEIGHT` `HY3_MX_DMA_SPLIT=2` | Run the routed experts in STATIC_MX (trn3 native FP8 MX matmul), add the two shard partials in the graph, and skip reloading the weights when consecutive blocks use the same expert |
+| Prefill MoE glue | `HY3_PREFILL_AG_TOPK` `HY3_MOE_ROWPAD` `HY3_MOE_PIPE` | All-gather only the top-k pairs. Pad the routing rows to a multiple of 2048, so the blockwise mapping takes the NKI path at every bucket (7168 included) |
+| Prefill attention | `HY3_PREFILL_ATTN_BLOCK=64` `HY3_PREFIX_ALIGN=64` `KV_SEGMENTS=[8192]` | View the contiguous BF16 request copy as 64-token blocks: the segmented kernel issues 2x fewer block DMAs (bit-identical). The prefix-cache hit is aligned to 64 tokens |
+| Prefill K/V write | `HY3_PREFILL_ROW_SCATTER` `HY3_PREFILL_BLOCK_SCATTER` `HY3_ROPE_TABLE` | Write the K/V cache in whole blocks; RoPE from a table |
+| Sparse prefill / decode | `HY3_SPARSE_PREFILL=0.0625` `HY3_SPARSE_DECODE=0.0625` `HY3_SPARSE_SELECT_EVERY=16` `HY3_SPARSE_*_PREP` `HY3_SPARSE_FLAT_GATHER` | Block selection from per-group K summaries (see `SPARSE_DECODE.md`). Layer-invariant preparation runs once per step, and the selection gathers run as flat `index_select` |
+| Decode attention | `HY3_DECODE_KVDP_FORK=8` `HY3_DECODE_KVDP_MIN_B=2` `HY3_SPARSE_KVDP` `HY3_SPARSE_KFROM_KERNEL` `HY3_SPARSE_KSUM_KERNEL` `HY3_SPARSE_KSUM_SELECT_ONLY` | KV data parallelism with the forked `attention_block_tkg_kvdp`: each of the 8 ranks sharing a KV head attends B/8 requests and writes all B new tokens. The sparse selection runs inside it. K comes back from the kernel, and an NKI kernel (`kernels/ksum_update.py`) updates the K summaries |
+| Decode MoE | `HY3_DECODE_MOE_FUSED` `HY3_DECODE_MOE_MX` `HY3_DECODE_HITS=0` | Fused decode MoE (PR #8, trn3 port with OCP FP8 activations) |
+| Host / launch | `HY3_IO_STABLE=2` `HY3_IO_STABLE_MAXB=0` `HY3_IO_STABLE_H2D=3` `HY3_DECODE_STEP_CONST` | Pooled per-graph output buffers and round-robin H2D input buffers (the runtime IO-ring cache then hits); constant per-step tensors |
+| Scheduler | `HY3_PREFILL_GANG=1` `HY3_GANG_MAX_WAIT_S` (4.5) `HY3_GANG_TAIL` `HY3_GANG_GATHER_S` `HY3_GANG_NO_TAIL` | Gang prefill (`vllm_neuron/vllm/core/scheduler.py`): hold arriving prefills briefly and run them back to back, so the running decodes stall fewer times per request |
+| Admission | `VLLM_NEURON_MAX_KV_CONCURRENT=24`, `NUM_BLOCKS=16000` | The worst-case cap (no prefix sharing) would admit 5 requests. The shared prefix is stored once, so 24 fit |
+
+`HY3_DECODE_KVDP_FORK` is a different implementation from `HY3_DECODE_KVDP` (`kvdp_attention.py`, the dense PD
+decode switch, which is unchanged). The fork runs the sparse selection inside KVDP; on trn3 with sparse decode it is
+the faster of the two. Set at most one of them.
+
+The other `HY3_*` flags in `model.py` are experiments that are off by default (see "Measured and not used" below).
+
+## Results (trn3, vllm-neuron 0.29.0.1.2.0 image, neuronx-cc 2.28, 2026-11-17)
+
+| C | GANG_WAIT | runs | output tok/s | TPOT P50 (ms) | TTFT P50 (s) | SLO |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 20 | 4.5 | 2 | 793-795 | 19.3-19.8 | 4.98 | pass in 2 of 2 |
+| 20 | 5.5 | 71 | 758-834, mean 776 | 17.8-19.7 | 5.57-6.65 | pass in 71 of 71 |
+| 24 | 4.5 | 4 | 879-907 | 20.6-21.4 | 5.0-5.25 | fail in 4 of 4 (TPOT) |
+| 24 | 5.5 | 13 | 855-892 | 19.5-20.5 | 6.0-6.96 | pass in 7 of 13 |
+
+- On the rebased branch (upstream e891054 merged, `serve_85k_trn3.sh`, gang wait 4.5), fresh compile:
+  - C = 20: 807 tok/s / TPOT 18.80 ms / TTFT 5.27 s, and 802 / 19.28 / 5.01, both pass.
+  - C = 24: 888 / 21.36 / 5.25 and 898 / 20.06 / 5.63, both fail on TPOT.
+  - MATH-500 97.0% (485/500), needle 12/12.
+  - The table above was measured on the same code before the rebase.
+- Prefix-cache hit rate is 92.1% and MTP acceptance 2.13-2.17 tokens per step in every run.
+- The best point that passes reliably is C = 20 at about 790 output tok/s per node. C = 24 gives about 880 tok/s with
+  TPOT right at the limit.
+- Accuracy with this configuration: MATH-500 no_think (temperature 0.9) 97.2% (486/500); needle (85k, 12 depths) 12/12.
+
+Decode profile at batch 24 (one target step = 28.1 ms + 3.7 ms for the MTP draft):
+- attention 10.5 ms, routed experts 11.8 ms, collectives 4.2 ms on TP0;
+- on pcore 1, 161 BF16 all-reduces of 786 KB take 3.95 ms and 160 all-to-alls take 1.4 ms;
+- torch ops of the sparse selection take 1.3 ms.
+
+At C = 24, TPOT P50 is about 14.8 ms of decode plus about 6-7 ms of prefill stalls per token.
+
+For reference, the trn2 PD results in this README are 1P1D chat end to end at C = 8 (TPOT 19.38 ms, about 192 output
+tok/s per node) and D-only at C = 10 (446 tok/s on the decode node).
+
+## Measured and not used
+
+Each of these was measured on trn3 and left off:
+- `HY3_DECODE_EXPERT_TP`, STATIC_MX decode experts with a balanced core split (`moe_tkg_mx_balanced*`)
+- the NKI router (`HY3_ROUTER_NKI`)
+- LNC-rebalanced prefill attention (`HY3_PREFILL_ATTN_BALANCE`, `HY3_PREFILL_ATTN_SPLIT`)
+- decode early exit (`HY3_DECODE_EARLY_EXIT`; inert below 32K buckets)
+- context-split decode (`HY3_DECODE_CTXSPLIT`)
+- the FP8 attention all-gather (`HY3_PREFILL_AG_FP8`)
+- the fused prefill QKV (`HY3_PREFILL_FUSED_QKV`; it conflicts with the coarse-block view)
+- the prefill MoE micro-batch split (`HY3_PREFILL_MOE_SPLIT=2`; its collectives do not overlap)
+- the fused shared expert (`HY3_DECODE_FUSED_SHARED`)
+- a greedy MTP draft
+- `sampling_dp_degree` 8 (the drafter recompiles under `fail_on_recompile`)
+- `NEURON_RT_CC_ALG_TYPES=^INTRA_RDH_ALG` (no ITL change on trn3)
+- the on-chip decode mask (`HY3_DECODE_POSID`; the mask load is overlapped)
+
+## Reproduce
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/serve_85k_trn3.sh                      # fresh compile ~50 min; GANG_WAIT=5.5 for C = 24
+bash scripts/bench_85k_slo.sh results/trn3_85k "20 24"
+```
